      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2528",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/db/db009d4dcba1804ca3ea2bb1e0515d976e11b76eced6c7091299f04c861d4bf2.png)\n\nSand is being dumped off a conveyor belt onto a pile at a rate of $3ft^{3}/min$. The sandpile is shaped like a right cone whose height and base diameter are always equal. At what rate is the height of the pile increasing when the pile is $6ft$ high?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
